    ],
    "description": "Two swordsmen, mock fight in Kalyana mandapa.  These are men from an agricultural caste in nearby village, who have inherited the privilege of playing these roles during the 6th day lila.; Minaksi temple, Avani Mula, 2007; Fighters are farmers, from Pandya-Vellalar jati, who have hereditary right to participate in 6th morning lila; Keywords: personnel, lilas"
  },
  {
    "Title": "Toyotomi Sutemaru and Toy Boat",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "",
    "Institution": "",
    "Source": "Money Hickman et al,  (u&quJapan's Golden Age: Momoyamated pl Dallas Museum of Art, 1996, scan of image on p. 63, fig. 49.",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only.",
    "Subject": "",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "Japan",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
    "Coverage": "1573-1615",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "634 w x 495, 60 ppi",
    "Collection": "Asian Takeout",
    "id": "4583",
    "filename": [
      "4583-toyotomi-sutemaru-and-toy-boat.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The boat is said to have been one of Sutemaru's toys.  Resembling a real boat, it has a small cabin at the helm and another at the stern.  A board with wheels is attached to the bottom of the boat so that it can be pulled."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Toyotomi Sutemaru",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Woudenberg, Annie",
    "Institution": "St. Olaf College",
    "Source": "Yoshiaki Shimizu, ed., p&quotJapan: The Shaping of Daimyo Culture 1185-1868tomi H Washington: National Gallery of Art, 1988, pl. 51.",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only.",
    "Subject": "Sculpture; Historical Figures; Children; Funeral art",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "Japan",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "678 w x 563 h, 150 ppi",
    "Collection": "Asian Takeout",
    "id": "4582",
    "filename": [
      "4582-toyotomi-sutemaru.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Portrait sculpture of Toyotomi Sutemaru (1589-1591), the first son of  Toyotomi Hideyoshi (1537-1598), died when he was just two years old.   Hideyoshi built Shounji in eastern Kyoto as the child's memorial temple.  This portrait was enshrined there.  Made of polychromed wood."
  },
