    "id": "4484",
    "filename": [
      "4484-chinese-yueyao-stoneware-offering-set-top-view.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Tray - 8 1/2\" w. Cups 1 7/8\" h x 3 1/2\" w. Five campanulate cups with slightly thickened rims and straight sided footrings fastened in a circle to the inside of a flaring short rim of a round tray with convex bottom containing a double beaded ring, concave base of the tray unglazed, pale yellowish brown glassy glaze, finely crazed, ending at the bottom in large droplets and pooling to a heavy bead.^^Uncovered from a site at the construction of the Nanzhang Airport, Giangsi Province 1934."
  },
