    "filename": [
      "4440-chinese-famille-rose-vases.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "5 1/2\" h. Tall, slender form with ovoid body, slender elongated neck flaring to an inverted lip with an overall incised design of flowers enameled in famille rose colors, red enamel seal mark of Qianlong and of the period."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Chinese Earthenware Tomb Vase",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Thorp Collection - Earlham College",
    "Institution": "Earlham College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "",
    "Subject": "Ceramics; Decorative Arts; Material Culture",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "China",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
    "Coverage": "Ming",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "1875 w x 2702 h, 300 ppi",
    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "4439",
    "filename": [
      "4439-chinese-earthenware-tomb-vase.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "7 1/2\" h. Bottle-form vase with pyriform body raised on a high splayed foot, the neck spreading outward near the top of culminating to an inverted scalloped collar which is surmounted by an inward tapered lip, two degenereated animal head handles are applied to the neck, molded with lobed bulbous portion above which is a band of vertical reeding with looped pendants, then a Greek key band followed finally by reeding continuing up to the collar, minutely crazed greenish-beige glaze carelessly applied."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Chinese Dingyao Vase",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Thorp Collection - Earlham College",
    "Institution": "Earlham College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only. Acknowledgement to be given to the ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project and to the college from whose collection the work comes. The individual college retains copyright to the work.",
    "Subject": "Arts; Ceramics; Decorative Arts; Material Culture",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "China",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
    "Coverage": "Yuan",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "1885 w x 2690 h, 300 ppi",
    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "4438",
    "filename": [
      "4438-chinese-dingyao-vase.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "5 5/5\" h. A baluster dorm with undulating foliate mouth and tall splayed foot ring , decorated in low relief, molded, with four separated panels of stiff lotus blossoms framed in arabesque reserve and divided by broad vertical columns which is all flanked by bands, top and bottom, of very thin rayed leaves, the bottom band continuing down the foot, extremely thin and light weight, the buff white glaze covers just the exterior and part of the interior, leaving the concave domed interior and the foot ring unglazed, white porcelaneous body."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Chinese Dingyao Twin Fish Bowl",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Thorp Collection - Earlham College",
    "Institution": "Earlham College",
