    "Collection": "Japanese Religion Images",
    "id": "4308",
    "filename": [
      "4308-prayer-strips-in-tamagawa.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "From the bridge over the Tamagawa stream that leads to Kobo Daishi's mausoleum one can see these wooden strips suspended above the stream so that the current washes across the bottom of the strips. On each strip is written the name of someone deceased, and the pure waters of this stream are said to purify their spirits wherever they may be in their afterlife journey."
  },
