    "Dimensions": "1280 w x 960",
    "Collection": "Religious Sites in Maharashtra",
    "id": "4273",
    "filename": [
      "4273-kailash-cave-temple-inner-sanctum.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This photo shows the steps leading up to the doorway of the Kailash Temple inner sanctum.  In the center of the small shrine room is a large Shiva lingam and yoni positioned to allow only a single line of people to circumambulate this aniconic representation of the divine.  This inner sanctum is continuously illuminated by one kerosene lamp."
  },
  {
