    "Collection": "Religious Sites in Maharashtra",
    "id": "4246",
    "filename": [
      "4246-ellora-buddhist-caves-balcony-entrance-detail.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "These auspicious celestial creatures, the male gandharva and two female apsarases appear to be floating or flying, just as they are described in mythological texts.  They live among the clouds but are associated also with water, sensuality, music, and dance.  Connected with Indra, king of the gods, the apsarases and gandharva depicted here might represent Indra's devotion to the Buddha and the many bodhisattvas."
  },
