    "filename": [
      "4243-ellora-buddhist-caves-chaitya-hall-entrance-far-vi.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This Chaitya Hall or place of assembly for monks and pilgrims is adorned with figures of amorous couples across the top, gandharvas and apsaras over the balcony doorway, and bodhisattvas at door level.  All of these figures are auspicious symbols, appropriately adorning a place of religious practice.  A popular destination for school field trips, children learn about the early history of these sites."
  },
