    "Collection": "Religious Sites in Maharashtra",
    "id": "4242",
    "filename": [
      "4242-ellora-buddhist-caves-panorama-view.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The Ellora Caves complex contains caves carved and used by Buddhists, Jains, and Hindus.  The twelve Buddhist caves at Ellora were excavated over a 500 years period extending from the second to seventh centuries CE.  These caves were used by monks who would have been supported by pilgrims and local people.  All the Ellora Caves are now maintained by the Archaeological Survey of India."
  },
