    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "1200 w  x  861 h, 150ppi",
    "Collection": "Asian Cultures Collection",
    "id": "4194",
    "filename": [
      "4194-hiroshima-peace-memorial-museum-art-by-survivors-2.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "A father carries his transformed son on his bicycle. A fa --  Explanation by the artist:  on hisA father carried home the corpse of his son, who had been exposed while demolishing buildings and was found on the riverbank at Koami-cho.\"  --  The artist was 13 years old at the time of the bombing, 60 when he drew this picture.  The scene depicted was 800 meters from the hypocenter.^^Collection Librarian: Amy Bryant. Please send comments or content corrections to Michael Thiedeman, Department of Art, Earlham College, Richmond, IN 47374 USA. email address: thiedmi@earlham.edu"
  },
