    "description": "Woodblock print; ink and colors on paper, framed under glass.^^A label on the back of the frame indicates that this print was purchased from Carolyn Staley Fine Prints, Seattle (one of the best Japanese print dealers in the USA). Museum records it entered the college collection in 1999. References: Helen Merritt and Nanako Yamada, Guide to Modern Japanese Woodblock Prints: 1900-1975. Honolulu: University of Hawaii Press, 1992, p. 142. and Amy Newland, ed. Printed to Perfection: Twentieth-century Japanese Prints from the Robert O. Muller Collection. Washington, D.C: Arthur M. Sackler Gallery and Amsterdam: Hotei Publishing, 2004.  AND Kendall H. Brown and Hollis Goodall-Cristante, Shin-hanga: New Prints in Modern Japan. Los Angeles: Los Angeles County Museum of Art in association with University of Washington Press, 1996."
