    "Collection": "Religious Sites in Maharashtra",
    "id": "3744",
    "filename": [
      "3744-aurangzeb-mosque-perfume-kiosk.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Outside many mosques in India, small shops sell perfumes and small ornaments.  Before prayer, all must perform ritual ablutions to purify oneself.  From an early period, perfumes have been associated with the idea of purification."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Aurangzeb Mosque, entranceway and view from outside",
