    ],
    "description": "A weary or infirm tourist or pilgrim can now sit in a sedan chair carried by two men hirerd to carry them up and down the walkway outside the caves."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Standing Buddha in Stupa, Chaitya Hall, cave 19",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Benton, Cathy",
    "Institution": "Lake Forest College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Copyright: April 2003 Cathy Benton. Images and content on this site are available for educational and research purposes, provided due recognition is given to the author. Transmission or reproduction of protected items beyond fair use requires the written permission of the photographer.",
    "Subject": "Buddhism; Figures; Sculpture",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "India",
    "Region": "South Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "01/01/2003",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "960 w x 1280 h",
    "Collection": "Religious Sites in Maharashtra",
    "id": "3721",
    "filename": [
      "3721-standing-buddha-in-stupa-chaitya-hall-cave-19.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This standing Buddha figure within a stupa-like structure is placed within a large chaitya hall, a cave where monks gathered for teaching and community ritual practices.  The straight, rigid form of this Buddha is reminiscent of figures of Jain tirthankaras, with whom early Buddhist monks shared many ideas and practices. The Buddha is depicted with the royal headdress of an aristocratic person but in the ascetic simplicity of an unclothed body."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ajanta Caves, pilgrims",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Benton, Cathy",
    "Institution": "Lake Forest College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Copyright: April 2003 Cathy Benton. Images and content on this site are available for educational and research purposes, provided due recognition is given to the author. Transmission or reproduction of protected items beyond fair use requires the written permission of the photographer.",
    "Subject": "Buddhism",
