    "Country": "India",
    "Region": "South Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "01/01/2003",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "960 w x 1280 h",
    "Collection": "Religious Sites in Maharashtra",
    "id": "3719",
    "filename": [
      "3719-buddha-seated-in-teaching-pose.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Seated in a throne-like setting, the Buddha is depicted with his hands in the teaching pose.  His feet rest on a lotus, symbol of enlightenment, and supernatural beings are carved around him, ostensibly also attending to his teachings.  The throne was constructed in the shape of a stupa within the cave, with ample room around it for monks and pilgrims to  circumambulate the image."
  },
