    "description": "Hiroshima today is a vibrant city, as seen in this image taken at the east end of the Peace Bridge across the Motoyasu river.  The Peace Memorial Museum is just several hundred meters away, near the other end of the Peace Bridge, and the A-bomb Dome, near the center of the A-bomb explosion, is perhaps half a mile up the river from the site where this photograph was taken.^^Collection Librarian:  Amy Bryant.  Please send comments or content corrections to Michael Thiedeman, Professor of Art, Earlham College, Richmond, IN  47374 USA.  email address:  thiedmi@earlham.edu"
