      "3557-muroji-014-haiden-hall-for-worship-seen-from-veran.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Directly in front of the Golden Hall, on the south side, is an open area, which is used for ceremonies.  The Mirokudo is on the western side of the open area, facing to the east.  The small building in this image is on the eastern side of the open area.  It is a  building for worship, used to honor the dragon of Ryuketsu Shrine, which is directly to the east of Muroji.   One of two straw dragons constructed as part of the Autumn Ryuketsu Shrine Festival is hung from a tree in the open area here at Muroji, while the other is hung by the river in front of the shrine, part of an interesting intermingling of rituals between the temple and the shrine.^^Editorial assistant: Joseph Augustin.  Collection librarian: Amy Bryant.  Please send comments, suggestions, or content corrections to Michael Thiedeman, Professor of Art, Earlham College, Richmond, IN 47374 USA.  email:  thiedmi@earlham.edu"
  },
