    "id": "3398",
    "filename": [
      "3398-muroji-021-five-story-pagoda-steps-leading-up-to-t.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The pagoda at Muroji is located on a level carved out of the hillside perhaps thirty feet or so (vertically) above the level of the Main Hall and its pool.  The stone steps shown here are to the left of the Main Hall and lead one directly up toward the pagoda, enhancing the sense of the height and floating quality of the pagoda, as one ascends the steps.^^Editorial assistant:  Sandy Augustin.  Collection Librarian:  Amy Bryant.  Please send any questions, comments, or content corrections to Michael Thiedeman, Professor of Art, Earlham College, Richmond, IN 47374 USA.  email address:  thiedmi@earlham.edu"
