    "filename": [
      "3327-byodoin-amida-buddha-view-2.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Again, the Amida figure in the Hoodo, Byodoin, as seen at eye level.  This image shows some of the apsara figures, high relief wood carvings, that are on the walls above and around the Amida figure.  Also, in the lower left, the altar in front ot the Amida, with its symbolic offerings to the Buddha.^^Byodoin, Hoodo, Uji^^Byodoin, Hoodo, Uji^^Editorial assistant:  Sandy Augustin.  Collection Librarian:  Amy Bryant.  Please send any questions, comments, or content corrections to Michael Thiedeman, Professor of Art, Earlham College, Richmond, IN 47374 USA.  email address:  thiedmi@earlham.edu"
  },
  {
    "Title": "Korean ceramics: Bottle, Buncheong ware.",
    "Creator": "unknown",
    "Contributor": "Thiedeman, Michael",
    "Institution": "Earlham College",
    "Source": "",
