    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "",
    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "2895",
    "filename": [
      "2895-fan-painting-whiling-away-the-summer.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The lotus, the fan and the robe pulled back from the neck all suggest the season of summer, and the subject of the scholar taking his ease. The lotus, the fan, and the robe pulled back from the neck all suggest the season of summer, and the subject of the scholar taking his ease in the garden during the summer has a long history. One famous example, not at all connected to this one in composition, is by Liu Guandao, probably dating from the early years of the Yuan dynasty (1279-1368).  The isolation and skillful arrangement of the three main elements of the composition, the pot of lotus, the seated figure, and the garden rock are typical of the Shanghai school, which was by far the most creative force in nineteenth century painting. The elongated face and the modulated and somewhat jerky lines of drapery are also seen in other works by Ren Xun. This is a convincing work by one of the major masters of the century. Ren Yi, who was indebted to Xun for some instruction but who soon surpassed him in popularity, did a very similar painting, also on a fan.  One could write a long essay on the differences and similarities between teacher and student."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Fan painting - Scholar in forest",
    "Creator": "Zhou Yong (active in Daoguang and Fengxian eras from 1821-1862)",
    "Contributor": "Collection of Groke Mickey",
    "Institution": "Watson Pavilion, Washington and Lee University",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only. Acknowledgement to be given to the ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project and to the college from whose collection the work comes. The individual college retains copyright to the work.",
    "Subject": "Arts; Calligraphy; Painting",
    "Language": "Chinese",
    "Country": "China",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
