    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "2902",
    "filename": [
      "2902-fan-painting-landscape.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Small landscape with inscription. Zhu Shilin is recorded in a dictionary of artists' names, but little more is known about him.  That source mentions his reputation in calligraphy-specifically his seal script-and says nothing about other subjects, but this small landscape is evidence for his skill in that genre. In this small space, the artist has created a feeling of great scale and distance, of a vast vista that spreads to the horizons beyond the mass of the mountain. This is a more successful and integrated landscape than a casual painter might accomplish."
  },
