    "description": "Also sometimes called the \"Wheel of Transmigration\". Ink and color on cloth painting depicting the six possible paths of Buddhist rebirth.  Rippling of image shows effects of keeping scrolls rolled up over long periods of time. Said to be from the Tibetan region of China."
