    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "2707",
    "filename": [
      "2707-under-the-umbrella.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Woodblock and copper etching, 30 X 21 inches, by Noboru Sawai. Image of a nude woman with body painting holding an umbrella while seated in a wheelbarrow. In the background are an old barn and a copse of trees on Vancouver Island, Canada. It a visual poem or riddle. The artist was a student of Toshi Yoshida before establishing his own studio in Canada."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Meeji",
    "Creator": "Fujita, F. (b. 1886)",
    "Contributor": "Flaten Art Museum",
