    "id": "2610",
    "filename": [
      "2610-japanese-double-gourd-shape-miniature-vase-with-de.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Height: 12 cm. This is a very fine quality piece of Satsuma-style ware made for export to the West in the late 19th century, a time when Japan was avidly promoting production of such wares to expand their economy internationally. The piece does not have the Satsuma mark, and hence should not be defined as \"Satsuma ware\" proper, but was made at a high quality kiln that imitated this popular export ware product. Probably from a kiln in Kyoto, Osaka, or Tokyo."
  },
