    ],
    "description": "Color woodblock, 7 X 9 1/4 inches, ink and color on paper. Odawara was a post town facing Sagami Bay. It is said that travelers on the Tokaido often stayed in Odawara for the night to rest in order to prepare for climbing the deadly Hakone pass the next day.l^^Originally purchased from Arts and Crafts, Yokoyama, Tokyo"
  },
  {
