      "2535-53-stations-of-the-tokaido-seki-station-48.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Color woodblock, 7 X 9 1/4 inches, ink and color on paper. Seki means 'checkpoint', and checkpoints were set up at strategic locations by the Tokugawa government to control traveling, police the road and prevent any unlawful activities. Hiroshige illustrates the arrival of a high ranking official accompanied by his entourage at Seki.^^Originally purchased from Arts and Crafts, Yokoyama, Tokyo"
  },
