    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "2501",
    "filename": [
      "2501-unglazed-footed-pot.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "From Ban Tamasat, third to first millennium BCE. Earthenware, H: 6 x 7 3/8 in. Unglazed earthenware was first produced in the third millennium in Southeast Asia. These unglazed vessels were used for domestic use and have been excavated in burials. They were constructed by coiling the clay, then smoothing with an anvil (a piece of wood or stone), rather than being wheel thrown."
  },
