    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "",
    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "2420",
    "filename": [
      "2420-bowl-containing-the-five-senses.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Ink and colored pencil on paper, 23-1/2 (L) x 18 (W) inches. A formal, symmetrical composition showing a golden bowl containing a mirror, representing vision (top center), a water-bearing conch representing the sense of taste (left), a pile of fruit indicating smell (right), and a pair of yellow cymbals signifying hearing (center).  These all rest on a swirling length of blue and red cloth representing the sense of touch.  A visionary landscape is drawn in the background.  This is skillfully rendered by an artist with prior training.^^Gift of Bruce Walker."
  },
