  {
    "Title": "Ideal Tibetan Government (Lotus Field) - another rendition",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Emison Art Museum",
    "Institution": "Depauw University",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only. Acknowledgement to be given to the ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project and to the college from whose collection the work comes. The individual college retains copyright to the work.",
    "Subject": "Arts; Painting; Buddhism",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "Tibet",
    "Region": "",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "",
    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "2416",
    "filename": [
      "2416-ideal-tibetan-government-lotus-field-another-rendi.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Ink and colored pencil on paper, 18 (L) x 23-1/2 (W) inches. This image depicts the ideal Tibetan government symbolized by 7 buildings.  The large palace with the yellow titled roof in the top right represents the Dalai Lama.  The smaller buildings represent the cabinet (kashag) and legislature.  Below are buildings said to represent the judiciary, departments of religion, education, agriculture, medicine and human welfare, and transportation.  At the very bottom is structure representing regional governors.  The sketch is signed \"Grant.\"  This image is less refined thtn the previous one and includes more landscape.^^Gift of Bruce Walker."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ideal Tibetan Government (Lotus Field)",
    "Creator": "Unknown",
