      "2404-amitabha-thangka.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Ground mineral pigment on cotton, silk, 64 (L)  x 34-1/2 (W)  inches. Amitabha is depicted here at the center of his paradise flanked by Avalokiteshwara and Padmasambhava.  Below are eight bodhisattavas, musicians, a devotee and two monks on lotuses.  Painted in the Central Tibetan style."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Sakaymuni (Thangka)",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Emison Art Museum",
    "Institution": "Depauw University",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only. Acknowledgement to be given to the ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project and to the college from whose collection the work comes. The individual college retains copyright to the work.",
    "Subject": "Arts; Painting; Buddhism",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "Tibet",
    "Region": "",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
