    "Subject": "Arts; Painting",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "Bali, Indonesia",
    "Region": "Southeast Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
    "Coverage": "20th century",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "",
    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "2306",
    "filename": [
      "2306-balinese-painting-on-cloth.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Signed in ink in margin: Made Sudana. Rice farmer.  Batuan, Bali - tourist painting.  (When western tourists request signatures on otherwise unsigned paintings at the point of sale, the seller may write a name in the margin which may be his own, or may be that of the painter.  Because there are only four personal names used in Bali for both men and women, there will be an enormous number of people alive at any given moment with exactly the same name.  In this case one quarter of every member of a Sudana lineage will be named Made.)"
  },
