      "2102-the-fishing-boat-front-close-up.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The Fishing Boat is a landscape foregrounding the nets and frames for harvesting seaweed, as well as fishing boats, the setting is probably in or near his lifelong home of Kobe.\n\nKawanishi is associated with the Sosaku hanga (creative printmaking) movement which flourished after the end of the Pacific War.  Unlike the Shin-hanga artists, who sold their designs to publishers employing professional specialist woodblock carvers and printers, Sosaku hanga artists took direct control of all aspects of printmaking, carving their own blocks and personally inking and printing their works."
  },
