      "2078-ceremonial-sword-and-sheath-full-view.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The ceremonial sword and sheath were important symbols of social status and male potency in traditional Paiwan culture in Taiwan. The sheath is decorated with human ancestral figures and a sacred mythological creature, the hundred-pace snake."
  },
