  {
    "Title": "The Prince Hikaru Genji holding an insect cage under drooping cherry blossoms",
    "Creator": "Kunisada Toyokuni III",
    "Contributor": "The Wriston Art Gallery. Lawrence University",
    "Institution": "",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only. Acknowledgement to be given to the ASIANetwork-Luce Asian\nArt in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project and to the college from whose collection the work comes. The individual college retains copyright to the work.",
    "Subject": "",
    "Language": "Punjabi",
    "Country": "Japan",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
    "Coverage": "Edo-Tokugawa",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "",
    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "1976",
    "filename": [
      "1976-the-prince-hikaru-genji-holding-an-insect-cage-und.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Kunisada was a pupil of Toyokuni I and one of the most famous and prolific figure artists of his day. Incorporating newer more brightly colored inks and innovative experimentation with the abstract quality of line and shadow Kunisada was successful with the public but many felt that he contributed to a decline in printmaking. Kunisada also collaborated with Hiroshige and developed his own series of the famous Tokaido but with the addition of his signature images of geisha and peasant women.\n\nA hero in Japanese literature, Prince Genji is a character believed to be created by the Japanese noblewoman Murasaki Shikibu in the early eleventh century. The tale of Genji, remarkable for its cast of characters and epic length follows the exploits of the handsome Prince throughout his life. Called by many the world's first novel, the tale is considered a classic in world literature. \n\nHere the Prince is pictured very much in the contemporary fashions of the Edo period holding a cricket cage, a common accoutrement among the leisure classes.\n"
  },
  {
    "Title": "The Courtesan Shigeoka of Okamotoya Brothel ",
