    "filename": [
      "1804-ikuta-jinja-banner-on-main-gate-of-ikuta-jinja.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This banner advertises an upcoming festival, on July 15th, that will feature the lighting of a thousand lanterns, the rope circle through which one may walk (chinuwa kuguri), and a purification rite aimed at \"countering obstacles, eliminating illness and vanquishing troubles.\""
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ikuta Jinja - Fortunes tied onto branches",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Gardiner, David L. , 1957-",
    "Institution": "Colorado College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only.  Acknowledgment to be given to the IDEAS image database and the photographer.  Photographer retains copyright.",
    "Subject": "Sites; Ritual; Shinto",
    "Language": "",
