    "id": "1792",
    "filename": [
      "1792-ikuta-jinja-torii-lined-path.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This short path leading to a small shrine within the Ikuta Jinja compound is lined by vermillion torii. Many Shinto shrines will have paths almost covered by torii in this manner. The torii are commonly erected on behalf of donors to the shrine."
  },
  {
