    "description": "Another photo of the tree that survived WWII."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ikuta Jinja - Plaque before enshrined tree",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Gardiner, David L. , 1957-",
    "Institution": "Colorado College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only.  Acknowledgment to be given to the IDEAS image database and the photographer.  Photographer retains copyright.",
    "Subject": "Sites; Shinto",
    "Language": "Japanese",
    "Country": "Japan",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "34.666667",
    "Longitude": "135.116667",
    "Date": "10/07/2002",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "640 w x 480 h, 72 ppi",
    "Collection": "Japanese Religion Images",
    "id": "1790",
    "filename": [
      "1790-ikuta-jinja-plaque-before-enshrined-tree.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This plaque in front of the tree with the himorogi says that the tree was over 500 years old when it was severely injured by burns received in the bombing of Kobe during WWII. However, even though shattered, it managed to stay alive, and so became revered as a symbol of rebirth and resuscitation. The plaque refers to it as a \"divine (kami) tree.\""
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ikuta Jinja - Old tree stump enshrined",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Gardiner, David L. , 1957-",
    "Institution": "Colorado College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only.  Acknowledgment to be given to the IDEAS image database and the photographer.  Photographer retains copyright.",
    "Subject": "Sites; Shinto",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "Japan",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "34.666667",
    "Longitude": "135.116667",
    "Date": "10/07/2002",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "640 w x 480 h, 72 ppi",
    "Collection": "Japanese Religion Images",
    "id": "1789",
    "filename": [
      "1789-ikuta-jinja-old-tree-stump-enshrined.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "An old tree stump within the Ikuta Jinja is herein celebrated by having its own enclosed space. Wrapped around it is a \"himorogi,\" which is a rope with stylized paper strips hanging from it that traditionally demarcates any sort of sacred space. Large old trees are frequently honored in this regard; the presence of the himorogi will prompt some Japanese visitors to place their hands together and bow briefly before such a tree. This particular tree, however, is unique because it survived the ravages of war. See the explanation accompanying the photo of the wooden plaque pictured in cocrejpn0087."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ikuta Jinja - An ema with a wish",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Gardiner, David L. , 1957-",
    "Institution": "Colorado College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only.  Acknowledgment to be given to the IDEAS image database and the photographer.  Photographer retains copyright.",
