      "1786-ikuta-jinja-an-ema-with-a-wish.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This ema, written in an accomplished calligraphic style, reads, \" For the curing of illness -- [Name] -- December 26, 1957. Please, somehow, help.\""
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ikuta Jinja - An ema with a wish",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Gardiner, David L. , 1957-",
    "Institution": "Colorado College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only.  Acknowledgment to be given to the IDEAS image database and the photographer.  Photographer retains copyright.",
    "Subject": "Sites; Ritual; Shinto",
    "Language": "Japanese",
    "Country": "Japan",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "34.666667",
    "Longitude": "135.116667",
    "Date": "10/07/2002",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "640 w x 480 h, 72 ppi",
    "Collection": "Japanese Religion Images",
    "id": "1787",
    "filename": [
      "1787-ikuta-jinja-an-ema-with-a-wish.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This ema reads, \" School: I pray that I may easily get into school.\" From a young age, Japanese children take what are often very competitive tests to enter both public and private schools. In the month of May, petitioners will post such ema around exam time, whether they seek to enter a junior  high, high school or college."
  },
