      "1788-ikuta-jinja-an-ema-with-a-wish.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This ema, signed by a man and a woman with different last names, says, \"May the two of us get along well this year.\" Appended to the left is also a note saying, \"Please also watch over littleTaro!!\""
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ikuta Jinja - Ema board at Ikuta Jinja",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Gardiner, David L. , 1957-",
    "Institution": "Colorado College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Materials may be used for educational, non-commercial purposes only.  Acknowledgment to be given to the IDEAS image database and the photographer.  Photographer retains copyright.",
    "Subject": "Sites; Shinto",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "Japan",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "34.666667",
    "Longitude": "135.116667",
    "Date": "02/07/2002",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "640 w x 480 h, 72 ppi",
    "Collection": "Japanese Religion Images",
    "id": "1782",
    "filename": [
      "1782-ikuta-jinja-ema-board-at-ikuta-jinja.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "To the right of the main hall stands this large structure on which visitors hang an \"ema,\" or a small wooden plaque with a string on which they have written a wish. The ema are purchased at the shrine for around 500 yen (four dollars), and as the other photos show they come in different styles. It is believed that placing one's wish in close proximity to the kami may enhance the chances of fulfillment."
  },
