    "Dimensions": "960 w x 1280 h",
    "Collection": "Religious Sites in Maharashtra",
    "id": "1717",
    "filename": [
      "1717-ellora-jain-caves-mahavira-shrine-entrance.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This shrine is dedicated to the 24th tirthankara, Mahavira, who is understood to have lived in the 6th or 5th century B.C.E.  Mahavira is depicted seated in the lotus position having achieved a state of pure liberation.  Other tirthankaras are depicted behind him."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ellora, Jain Caves, tirthankara with animals",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Benton, Cathy",
    "Institution": "Lake Forest College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Copyright: April 2003 Cathy Benton. Images and content on this site are available for educational and research purposes, provided due recognition is given to the author. Transmission or reproduction of protected items beyond fair use requires the written permission of the photographer.",
    "Subject": "Jainism; Figures; Sites; Sculpture; Male; Animals",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "India",
    "Region": "South Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "01/01/2003",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "960 w x 1280 h",
    "Collection": "Religious Sites in Maharashtra",
    "id": "1716",
    "filename": [
      "1716-ellora-jain-caves-tirthankara-with-animals.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Demonstrating the Jain practice of non-violence, this tirthankara is depicted with animals and insects at his feet.  Near his right leg is a scorpion.  Refusing to take life, even in microscopic forms, to make cloth, he lives throughout the year as a \"digambara\" monk, clothing himself with the sky. Bits of ancient red paint remain on this figure."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ellora, Jain Caves, yakshini guardian",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Benton, Cathy",
    "Institution": "Lake Forest College",
    "Source": "",
    "Rights": "Copyright: April 2003 Cathy Benton. Images and content on this site are available for educational and research purposes, provided due recognition is given to the author. Transmission or reproduction of protected items beyond fair use requires the written permission of the photographer.",
    "Subject": "Jainism; Sites; Figures; Sculpture",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "India",
    "Region": "South Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "01/01/2003",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "960 w x 1280 h",
    "Collection": "Religious Sites in Maharashtra",
    "id": "1715",
    "filename": [
      "1715-ellora-jain-caves-yakshini-guardian.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Seated opposite her male counterpart, this protective yakshini, Siddhayika, acts as an entrance protector to the second floor shrine to Mahavira.  She sits on a lion under the canopy of a mango tree heavy with fruit.  Identified with the fertility of the earth, this female earth spirit holds a child on her lap (now missing its head)."
  },
  {
    "Title": "Ellora, Jain Caves, Yaksha Elephant detail",
    "Creator": "",
    "Contributor": "Benton, Cathy",
    "Institution": "Lake Forest College",
    "Source": "",
