      "1707-ellora-ganapati-temple-inner-sanctum-doorway.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The small inner shrine of the temple is set off from the rest of the temple by this decorated doorway.  Devotees ring the bell to announce their presence to the god and then step over the door frame to perform their puja and receive darshan.  Barely visible just inside the door is the image of the elephant-faced deity."
  },
