    "filename": [
      "1401-character-kuan-or-guan.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Five calligraphic renderings of the character, 'kuan/guan,' meaning 'to look at, see or behold'.  Guide to each character: a. Wang Hsi-chih, 'Essay on Yueh I'  b. Chih-yung, 'The Thousand Character Essay (detail)', late 6th century.  From 'Shoseki meihin sokan 6,' no. 69; p. 22.  c. Ou-yang Hsun, 'Inscription on the Sweet Wine Spring in the Chiu-cheng Palace, 632.'  d. Li Yung (678-747 AD) 'Epitaph for the Yun-hui general, Li Ssu-hsun,' after 739.  e. Yen Chen-ch'ing, 'Record of the Altar of the Goddess Ma-ku' ; 771 AD"
  },
