    "Subject": "Arts; Decorative Arts; Home Life",
    "Language": "",
    "Country": "Japan",
    "Region": "East Asia",
    "Latitude": "",
    "Longitude": "",
    "Date": "",
    "Coverage": "",
    "Type": "Still Image",
    "Dimensions": "",
    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "1257",
    "filename": [
      "1257-lacquer-tray-top-view.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "This simple rectangular tray is lacquered over a finely joined wooden core in numerous layers of colored lacquer to simulate pudding stone. Japanese lacquer artists excelled at simulating different materials in their craft, including metals, various stone finishes, wood grain and shells. 11 x 8.25 inches; height 1/2 inch.^^Gift of William Kelly."
  },
