    "id": "938",
    "filename": [
      "938-great-egret.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "Possibly a work by a follower of Zhao Mengfu. The painting is very fine, probably cut down from a larger composition and now in a Japanese mounting. The subject and composition are inspired by Song bird-and-flower painting, but the slightly stylized qualities suggest a later date, possibly as early as the late Yuan, but also possibly Ming dynasty. To view a detail of the egret, click on related record below."
  },
