    "Collection": "ASIANetwork-Luce Asian Art in the Undergraduate Curriculum Project",
    "id": "910",
    "filename": [
      "910-three-friends-of-winter.jpg"
    ],
    "description": "The subject is not really the three friends since, instead of pine, bamboo, and plum, we have plum, bamboo, two birds, a peony and a rock. The inscription gives Yun Bing, the daughter of Yun Shouping, as the artist, but given the inaccurate descriptive title, the attribution to Yun Bing is debatable. 38 x 16 1/16 inches. Ink and colors on silk."
  },
